                                                                                bacterium, designated as AM1114T, was isolated from a deep-sea hydrothermal
         Valorization des                                                       vent sample from the East-Pacific Rise (EPR 13m N). The cells were long
         Produits5 , IFREMER,                                                   (3–10 µm) rods, motile with peritrichous flagella, and exhibited a Gram-
         Centre de Brest, BP 70,
         29280 Plouzane! , France
                                                                                negative cell wall ultrastructure. In the late stationary phase of growth, cells
     2
                                                                                formed an ovoid, refractile, terminal endospore. They grew at 45–65 mC
         UMR 7622, Laboratoire
         de Biologie Cellulaire et
                                                                                inclusive (optimum 55–60 mC ; doubling time approx. 45 min), at pH 45–80
         Mole! culaire du                                                       inclusive (optimum pH 75–80) and at sea salt concentrations of 20–60 g lN1
         De! veloppement, 7 quai                                                inclusive (optimum 25–30 g lN1). Strain AM1114T was an obligately
         St Bernard, 75252 Paris
         Ce! dex 05, France
                                                                                heterotrophic bacterium able to ferment a mixture of 20 amino acids, complex
     3
                                                                                proteinaceous substrates (such as yeast extract, brain–heart infusion or
         Laboratoire de
         Microbiologie
                                                                                peptone), and carbohydrates such as glucose, galactose or maltose. The main
         Industrielle, URCA, UFR                                                fermentation products on glucose/yeast extract/peptone/sulfur medium were
         Sciences, BP 1039,                                                     hydrogen, carbon dioxide, butyrate, ethanol, acetate, formate and L-alanine.
         Moulin de la Housse,
         51687 Reims Cedex 2,
                                                                                The GMC content of the genomic DNA (determined by thermal denaturation)
         France                                                                 was 242O1 mol %. Phylogenetic analyses of the 16S rRNA gene located the
     6
