                                                                                strain within cluster XI of the lineage encompassing the genus Clostridium and
         Environnement Profond,                                                 related genera (sensu Collins et al., 1994), in the bacterial domain. On the basis
         Direction des Ressources                                               of 16S rDNA sequence comparisons and physiological and biochemical
         Oce! aniques, IFREMER,
         Centre de Brest, BP 70,
                                                                                characteristics, it is proposed that the isolate should be described as a novel
         29280 Plouzane! , France                                               genus, namely Caminicella gen. nov., of which Caminicella sporogenes sp. nov.
                                                                                is the type species. The type strain is AM1114T (l DSM 14501T l CIP 107141T).



