                                                                                                                                                    Morphological and physiological characteristics
                                                                                                                                                    Scanning electron microscopy and phase-contrast mi-
                                                                                                                                                    croscopy indicated that cells of isolate AM1114T were
                                                                                                                                                    thin, straight to slightly curved rods approximately
                                                                                                                                                    0n5–0n7 µm wide and 3–10 µm long (mean length, 6 µm)
                                                                                                                                                    during the exponential phase of growth. They ap-
                                                                                                                                                    peared as single cells (Fig. 2, top) or in pairs. Under
                                                                                                                                                    unfavourable growth conditions and in the stationary
                                                                                                                                                    phase of growth, cells elongated ; occasionally, cells
                                                                                                                                                    that were 17 µm long were observed. The cells stained
                                                                                                                                                    Gram-negative, and electron microscopy of thin sec-
                                                                                                                                                    tions of strain AM1114T revealed the presence, in the
                                                                                                                                                    cell wall, of a thin peptidoglycan layer characteristic of
                                                                                                                                                    Gram-negative bacteria (Fig. 2, bottom). Moreover,
                                                                                                                                                    the KOH reaction was positive, confirming the Gram-
                                                                                                                                                    negative type of AM1114T cells. In the late stationary
                                                                                                                                                    phase of growth, cells formed an ovoid, refractile,
                                                                                                                                                    terminal endospore (Fig. 2, top). Both non-sporulated
                                                                                                                                                    and sporulated cells were motile by means of peritri-
                                                                                                                                                    chous flagella.
                                                                                                                                                    This isolate is not an exception among Gram-negative
                                                                                                                                                    bacteria of the Firmicutes. In fact, the genus Clostri-
                                                                                                                                                    dium sensu lato is polyphyletic and is related phylo-
                                                                                                                                                    genetically to several Gram-negative-staining taxa (for
                                                                                                                                                    example Broda et al., 2000 ; Wery et al., 2001b).
                                                                                                                                                    Strain AM1114T grew at 45–65 mC, the optimum being
